# Volt Pitch components

Kids football coaching app, ages 9–12. Dark mode first. Keep existing behavior when restyling.

Colors: background `#0D1117`, surfaces `#161B22` / `#1C2128`, border `#2A2F36`, lime `#39FF14` or `#00FF85`, cyan `#00E5FF`, orange `#FF6B00`, text `#FFFFFF` / `#A0AEC0`. Headlines Poppins ExtraBold. Body Nunito or Poppins. Cards 16–24px radius. Buttons 12px radius. Large, high-contrast, tappable targets.

## Buttons

- Primary: fill `#FF6B00`, white text, slight orange glow, rounded.
- Secondary: outlined or filled neon lime.
- Do not use Streamlit’s default blue or gray for actions.

## Cards

- Dark surface, subtle border. Active or in-progress cards get a neon lime border or glow.
- Bold title, then secondary text. One clear action.

## Progress and charge

- Progress is a glowing neon lime **Charge Level** bar, not a plain gray bar.
- Skill paths may use thin circuit-style connectors between nodes.
- XP and level read as energy: lime number, short spark or motion accent on success.

## Bottom navigation

- Dark bar, at most 5 items. Default set: Home, Train, Challenges, Profile.
- Active icon is neon lime with a glow. Inactive icons use secondary text.

## Characters

Use this for every player avatar, skill-path character, and celebration screen.

- Soft 3D stylized kids, ages 9–12. Not flat 2D. Not realistic.
- Athletic kids: slightly oversized heads, big expressive eyes, friendly confident faces. Not babyish or overly cute.
- Clean soft 3D, like a modern game character. Smooth shading, subtle subsurface scattering. No hard cel shading.
- Inclusive and natural. Light skin reads Caucasian. Dark skin reads African. Hair styles are short, curly, and ponytail. Hair colours are black, brown, and blonde. Genders are M and F.
- Kit: dark black jersey and shorts. Neon lime `#39FF14` on the collar, side stripes, number, and logo. Cyan `#00E5FF` on socks, headbands, and small details.
- Poses are dynamic: running, dribbling, controlling the ball, or celebrating. Not a static mascot stance.
- Subtle neon rim light. Clean and polished, with very little texture noise.
- Cool, energetic, and empowering. Kids who belong on a modern pitch.

Creator choices are gender, skin, hair style, hair colour, boots, and nickname. The pictured kit is the Volt kit: black, lime, and cyan. Boots are black or orange.

## Training and skill path

A glowing circuit on a dark pitch.

- Completed nodes: bright neon lime, checkmark, glow.
- Current node: cyan or orange pulse.
- Locked nodes: dimmed.
- Connectors light up only through completed progress.
- Bottom: next-drill card and one large orange **Start Drill** button.
- Copy uses Charge, Power Up, and names like Electric Dribbler.
- Characters on the path use the soft 3D kid style, in a running or dribbling pose.

## Drill complete and level-up

A power surge for ages 9–12. Full-screen or modal on a dark background with electric streaks.

- Headline is **CHARGE UP!** or **POWER SURGE!** in neon lime, large and bold.
- Soft spark or glow animation. No clutter.
- Show XP gained. Show the streak when one exists.
- The cheering kid uses the soft 3D character style, in a celebration pose, with the Volt kit.
- One large continue button: hot orange or neon lime, white or dark text that stays readable.

## Section complete level-up

The Situational Coach power surge, for ages 9–12, when a section is finished. It is a popup over the pitch, on a dark background with electric streaks and a short surge sound.

- Small line **POWER SURGE!** then a huge neon lime **CHARGE UP**.
- A glowing cyan energy orb and the player’s own avatar, in the soft 3D Volt kit.
- Show the bonus as **XP BOOST +500 XP**.
- Line: **YOU'RE UNSTOPPABLE!** then “Keep pitching. Keep winning.”
- One large **BACK TO THE PITCH** button: lime-to-yellow fill, dark text that stays readable.
